@doc smysl/0.1 {
  id: v/f5
  intent: dataset-analysis
  lang: en
  granularity: { profile: default }
  roots: [f/regional-skew]
}

@artifact-ref a/notebook { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: "analysis/2026-06-regional.ipynb" }, sha256: "9f2c1ab4", cells: 34 }
~ The notebook that produced every table and figure below.

@artifact-ref a/extract { status: cited, source: { kind: url, ref: "s3://warehouse/orders/2026-06/" }, rows: 4812993, format: "parquet" }
~ The June order extract the analysis was run against.

@data t/latency-by-region { status: measured, source: { kind: file, ref: "analysis/tables/latency_by_region.csv", captured: 2026-06-30 }, columns: ["region", "p50_ms", "p95_ms", "orders"], rows: 6, x.stats/method: "empirical-quantile" }
~ Checkout latency by region, June 2026, six regions.

Region-level p50 and p95 over 4.8 million orders, quantiles computed
empirically rather than from a fitted distribution because the tail is the
part under examination and a fit would smooth exactly the shape in question.

@data t/orders-by-hour { status: measured, source: { kind: file, ref: "analysis/tables/orders_by_hour.csv", captured: 2026-06-30 }, columns: ["hour_utc", "orders", "eu_share"], rows: 24, x.stats/method: "count" }
~ Order volume by hour of day with the European share of each hour.

@evidence e/eu-west-tail { status: measured, source: { kind: file, ref: "analysis/tables/latency_by_region.csv", captured: 2026-06-30 } }
~ eu-west p95 is 610 ms against a 250 ms median across the other five regions.

@evidence e/eu-west-share { status: measured, source: { kind: file, ref: "analysis/tables/orders_by_hour.csv", captured: 2026-06-30 } }
~ eu-west contributes 38 per cent of orders in its four busiest hours.

@claim c/tail-is-regional { status: derived, grounds: [e/eu-west-tail], deps: [t/latency-by-region] }
~ The latency tail is concentrated in one region rather than spread evenly.

Five of six regions sit within forty milliseconds of each other at p95, and
the sixth sits two hundred and fifty above the next worst, which is a gap no
reasonable pooling of the six would produce by chance.

@claim c/concentration-matters { status: derived, grounds: [e/eu-west-share], deps: [t/orders-by-hour] }
~ The affected region carries enough volume for the tail to move the global figure.

@hypothesis h/sampling-artefact { status: speculative }
~ The gap could be an artefact of uneven instrumentation coverage.

@evidence e/coverage { status: measured, source: { kind: metric, ref: "trace.coverage_by_region", captured: 2026-06-30 } }
~ Trace coverage is between 97 and 99 per cent in all six regions.

@claim c/coverage-even { status: derived, grounds: [e/coverage] }
~ Instrumentation coverage is even enough to rule out a sampling artefact.

@finding f/regional-skew { status: inferred, grounds: [c/tail-is-regional, c/concentration-matters, c/coverage-even] }
~ The global p95 is dominated by one region, not by a fleet-wide regression.

@rel c/coverage-even --rebuts--> h/sampling-artefact { weight: 0.9 }
@rel a/notebook --backs--> t/latency-by-region
@rel a/extract --backs--> t/orders-by-hour
@rel t/latency-by-region --warrant--> c/tail-is-regional
@rel c/tail-is-regional --causes--> f/regional-skew
